<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
  A sapient mech can't use [AV] Mechanoid Skins' own skin-changer gizmo, because that gizmo
  only appears on a pawn whose render tree still matches AV_MechSkinsRenderTree (or one
  tagged compatible via its own HasSkinCompatibleRendertree mod extension) - and Big and
  Small always substitutes its own BS_HumanlikeAnimal tree onto every sapient pawn during
  conversion (HumanlikeAnimalGenerator.SetRenderTree), so that check always fails.

  Forcing AV_MechSkinsRenderTree itself back on hits the same crash already found and
  reverted for Lady's original "HumanlikeMech" tree (see HumanlikeAnimalSettings_MechQueens.
  xml): AV Mechanoid Skins' own body node, PawnRenderNode_MechanoidSkin, extends
  PawnRenderNode_AnimalPart and calls Pawn.ageTracker.CurKindLifeStage directly, which
  throws for a pawn Big and Small has also made RaceProps.Humanlike - confirmed by
  decompile, not just by analogy.

  This tree instead mirrors BS_HumanlikeAnimal's own shape - every other node is still Big
  and Small's own class, unchanged (Wounds/Pack/Firefoam/Carried) - and only swaps the Body
  node's class for SapientMechanoidFix.PawnRenderNode_SapientMechSkin, a subclass of Big and
  Small's own PawnRenderNode_HAnimalBody (the humanlike-safe body node BS_HumanlikeAnimal
  itself already uses, which resolves its graphic through Big and Small's own
  original-animal-kindDef lookup instead of ageTracker, sidestepping the crash entirely). It
  defers to Big and Small's own graphic resolution first and only overlays an [AV] Mechanoid
  Skins design on top if the pawn has one chosen - see PawnRenderNode_SapientMechSkin.cs and
  MechanoidSkinRenderSupport.cs.

  Registered onto specific mechs (currently just the War Queen) via renderTreeWhitelist in
  HumanlikeAnimalSettings_MechQueens.xml - scoped per-ThingDef, not a global substitution,
  so a mistake here can't take down every pawn's rendering the way forcing a tree globally
  once did. The HasSkinCompatibleRendertree mod extension below is [AV] Mechanoid Skins' own
  documented mechanism for a foreign render tree to declare itself capable of applying a
  skin on its own - exactly this situation.

  MayRequire means this whole def is entirely inert without [AV] Mechanoid Skins installed -
  nothing anywhere ever references it in that case.
  -->
  <PawnRenderTreeDef MayRequire="Veltaris.MechanoidSkins">
    <defName>SapientMechanoidFix_MechSkinRenderTree</defName>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="AV_MechanoidSkins.HasSkinCompatibleRendertree">
        <IsSkinCompatible>true</IsSkinCompatible>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <root Class="PawnRenderNodeProperties_Parent">
      <debugLabel>Root</debugLabel>
      <tagDef>Root</tagDef>
      <children>
        <li>
          <debugLabel>Body</debugLabel>
          <tagDef>Body</tagDef>
          <nodeClass>SapientMechanoidFix.PawnRenderNode_SapientMechSkin</nodeClass>
          <workerClass>BigAndSmall.PawnRenderNodeWorker_HumanlikeAnimalBody</workerClass>
          <useRottenColor>true</useRottenColor>
          <children>
            <li>
              <debugLabel>Wounds</debugLabel>
              <nodeClass>BigAndSmall.PawnRenderNode_HAnimalPart</nodeClass>
              <workerClass>PawnRenderNodeWorker_OverlayWounds</workerClass>
              <overlayLayer>Body</overlayLayer>
              <useGraphic>false</useGraphic>
              <pawnType>Any</pawnType>
              <baseLayer>3</baseLayer>
            </li>
            <li>
              <debugLabel>Pack</debugLabel>
              <nodeClass>BigAndSmall.PawnRenderNode_HAnimalPack</nodeClass>
              <workerClass>BigAndSmall.PawnRenderNodeWorker_HAnimalPack</workerClass>
              <rotDrawMode>Fresh, Rotting</rotDrawMode>
              <pawnType>Any</pawnType>
              <baseLayer>5</baseLayer>
            </li>
            <li>
              <debugLabel>Firefoam</debugLabel>
              <nodeClass>BigAndSmall.PawnRenderNode_HAnimalPart</nodeClass>
              <workerClass>PawnRenderNodeWorker_OverlayFirefoam</workerClass>
              <overlayLayer>Body</overlayLayer>
              <useGraphic>false</useGraphic>
              <pawnType>Any</pawnType>
              <baseLayer>10</baseLayer>
            </li>
          </children>
        </li>
        <li Class="PawnRenderNodeProperties_Carried">
          <debugLabel>Carried thing</debugLabel>
          <workerClass>PawnRenderNodeWorker_Carried</workerClass>
          <pawnType>Any</pawnType>
        </li>
      </children>
    </root>
  </PawnRenderTreeDef>

</Defs>
